  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BEL: Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration for Migrants Stranded on the Territory of Belarus</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM will render Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration (AVRR) services to the most vulnerable migrants stranded in Belarus who wish to return home and against whom no criminal proceedings have been instituted, nor has a decision been taken on forced deportation, unless such a decision is revoked. All returns will be implemented strictly following the IOM Guidance Notes and Standard Operating Procedures, and applicable international law, including the principle of non-refoulement, rights-based and protection-sensitive approach, best interests of the child, and coordinated with the IOM office in each country of origin well in advance. IOM will facilitate voluntary return to countries where conditions for return are met based on the IOM Voluntary Returns Suspension and Pre-Return Clearances List.</narrative>
  </description>
